INVESTIGATIVE SUMMARY & ENTITY RECORD
On February 14, 2026, Special Agents Marcus Vance and Elena Rostova interviewed CHS-4819 regarding the narcotics distribution and money laundering network operating under the moniker "Eastern Seaboard Logistics Group."
Entity Declarations & Cross-References:
Primary Target: Victor "The Mechanic" Vance (DOB: 11/14/1979, SSN: XXX-XX-4819, Alias: "Mechanic-X")
Corporate Entity: Apex Freight Logistics LLC (EIN: 84-9102847, Registered Address: 1404 Industrial Parkway, Newark, NJ)
Offshore Shell Company: Ironclad Holdings Ltd. (Nevis Registration: NV-2023-8819)
Logistics Node: Pier 42, Port Newark Container Terminal (Lat/Long: 40.6721° N, 74.1482° W)
Narrative Details:
CHS-4819 provided explicit details concerning the structural hierarchy of Apex Freight Logistics LLC. CHS-4819 stated that Apex Freight Logistics LLC operates as a primary front company for receiving maritime cargo containers originating from Guayaquil, Ecuador. Victor Vance serves as the operational director but maintains no legal ownership on paper. Legal documentation lists Vance's sister, Clara Vance-Moreno, as the Managing Member.
According to CHS-4819, illicit cargo arrives under falsified manifest bill of lading #BL-EC-90184-X listed as "Commercial Refrigeration Units." Once offloaded at Pier 42 in Port Newark, the containers are picked up by Apex Freight Logistics commercial drivers operating 2023 Freightliner Cascadia trucks (VIN: 1FUJGLDR8PLKP9012, NJ License Plate: X78-PL9).
Payments for transport and offload crews are routed through Ironclad Holdings Ltd., an entity registered in Nevis. CHS-4819 observed wire transfers executed from Ironclad Holdings Ltd. to domestic bank accounts held at First National Commerce Bank (Routing: 021000021, Account: 4910-8819-02) under the disguise of "Equipment Lease Payments."
